   "text": {
    "L1": "A pictograph uses pictures to show data in a simple way.",
    "L2": "First, read the key. It tells us how many things one picture stands for.",
    "L3": "Here, one cloud picture stands for five rainy days.",
    "L4": "July has four cloud pictures, so we multiply four by five.",
    "L5": "Four times five is twenty, so July had twenty rainy days.",
    "L6": "A half picture also matters: it stands for half of the key's number.",
    "L7": "Do not count pictures alone. Use the key, then multiply."
   },
